<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paraguayan War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1864">1864</a>–<a href="/years/1870">1870</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Paraguayan War, fought from 1864 to 1870, was a conflict between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraguay">Paraguay</a> and the Triple Alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a>. It ended in Paraguay's defeat and catastrophic loss of population. For the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a> it was a victory financed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> revenues, but it turned the army into a professional force whose officers later overthrew the monarchy in 1889.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paraguayan-war.jpg" alt="Paraguayan War" width="297" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Inkratt · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Escenas_de_la_Guerra_de_la_Triple_Alianza.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
